[{"text":"(5.1.3) $$\\cdots\\xrightarrow{H}Q^{2m-1}_{2m-1+k}\\xrightarrow{P}\\pi^{2m-1}_{2m-1+k}\\xrightarrow{E^2}\\pi^{2m+1}_{2m+1+k}\\xrightarrow{H}Q^{2m-1}_{2m-2+k}\\xrightarrow{P}\\cdots.$$","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"The computations of the $k$-stem groups are done by use of the following","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"Computing Diagram mod A","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"Here the group $Q^{2m-1}_{2m-1+k}$ has to be fiexed in advance by the IJ$\\Delta$-sequence of Theorem 2.2. For $k<107$, $Q^{2m-1}_{2m-1+k}$ contains extra elements","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"(5.1.4) $$w=IP(\\iota)\\in Q^{2m-1}_{18m-5},\\qquad a_1\\in Q^{6m-3}_{18m-8},\\qquad a_2\\in Q^{18m-5}_{54m-8}$$","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"[p. 44]","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"of section 4.5. Let $\\overline{Q}{}^{2m-1}_{2m-1+k}$ be the quotient over the subgroup spanned by (5.1.4). Then the invariants mod A is obtained by the following exact sequence.","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"(5.1.5) $$\\cdots\\xrightarrow{J}\\pi^{6m+1}_{2m+1+k}\\xrightarrow{\\Delta}\\pi^{6m-1}_{2m-1+k}\\xrightarrow{I}\\overline{Q}{}^{2m-1}_{2m-1+k}\\xrightarrow{J}\\pi^{6m+1}_{2m+k}\\xrightarrow{\\Delta}\\pi^{6m-1}_{2m-2+k}\\xrightarrow{I}\\cdots.$$","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"In the case $m=1$, $H:\\pi^3_{3+k}\\to Q^1_k$ is bijective for $k\\ne0$. Then the group $\\pi^3_{3+k}$ will be computed directly by the following sequence","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"(5.1.6) $$\\cdots\\xrightarrow{H_p}\\pi^7_{4+k}\\xrightarrow{\\Delta}\\pi^5_{2+k}\\xrightarrow{G}\\pi^3_{3+k}\\xrightarrow{H_p}\\pi^7_{3+k}\\xrightarrow{\\Delta}\\pi^5_{1+k}\\xrightarrow{G}\\cdots,$$","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"derived from Theorem 2.4. Remark that the sequence (5.1.6) is exact except the case $k=11$.","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"In the computating diagram, many numbers of generators in $Q^{2m-1}_i$ are given as stable type invariants $$Q^m(\\xi)\\in Q^{2m-1}_{6m-1+k}\\quad\\textit{or}\\quad\\overline{Q}{}^m(\\xi)\\in Q^{2m-1}_{6m+k}\\quad\\textit{for}\\quad\\xi\\in\\pi^S_k$$ given in (2.4.1) or (2.4.2). We represent such generators by corresponding roman charactors. The following (5.1.7) is the list of stable type invariants correponding to the stable generators in (5.1.1).","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"(5.1.7) Invariants $Q^m(\\xi)$ and $\\overline{Q}{}^m(\\xi)$ for $\\xi\\in\\pi^S_k$, $k\\le55$.","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"$k$ · 0 · 3 · 7 · 10 · 13 · 20 · 23 · 26 · 29 · 30 · 36 · 37 · 38","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"$\\xi$ · $\\iota$ · $\\alpha_1$ · $\\alpha_2$ · $\\beta_1$ · $\\alpha_1\\beta_1$ · $\\beta_1^2$ · $\\alpha_1\\beta_1^2$ · $\\beta_2$ · $\\alpha_1\\beta_2$ · $\\beta_1^3$ · $\\beta_1\\beta_2$ · $\\epsilon'$ · $\\epsilon_1$","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"$Q^m(\\xi)$ · $i$ · $a$ · $a_2$ · $b$ · $ab$ · $b^2$ · $ab^2$ · $b_2$ · $ab_2$ · $b^3$ · $bb_2$ · $e'$ · $e_1$","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"$\\overline{Q}{}^m(\\xi)$ · · · · $B$ · $AB$ · $B^2$ · $AB^2$ · $B_2$ · $AB_2$ · $B^3$ · $BB_2$ · $E'$ · $E_1$","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"$k$ · 39 · 40 · 42 · 45 · 45 · 46 · 47 · 49 · 50 · 52 · 55","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to unstable"},{"text":"$\\xi$ · $\\alpha_1\\beta_1\\beta_2$ · $\\beta_1^4$ · $\\epsilon_2$ · $\\varphi$ · $\\alpha_1\\epsilon_2$ · $\\beta_1^2\\beta_2$ · $\\beta_1\\epsilon'$ · $\\alpha_1\\beta_1^2\\beta_2$ · $\\beta_1^5$ · $\\beta_2^2$ · $\\alpha_1\\beta_2^2$","section":"5.1 3-primary Groups, stable to 